implementationPlan.description:
Reference docs. Before writing, read the landed facts:
- packages/moe-daemon/src/types/schema.ts: Epic.finalTaskId;
- src/delivery/policy.ts: isEpicFinalTask. No epic means final. A designation counts only while it names an existing task of the same epic that is not ARCHIVED, and then only that task is final. Otherwise the highest order among the epic's non-ARCHIVED tasks wins, ties counting;
- src/state/validators.ts: validateEpicUpdates (string, at most 200 chars, trimmed, '' clears);
- src/tools/updateEpic.ts: assertDesignatable, which refuses an id that names no task, a task of another epic, or an ARCHIVED task;
- the update_epic section of docs/MCP_SERVER.md.

docs/SCHEMA.md:
(a) In '## Epic', add finalTaskId?: string; after order: number;, with a comment in the file's style. It is the epic's designated final (integration-and-hardening) task, set or cleared with moe.update_epic { epicId, finalTaskId } ('' clears). It counts only while it names an existing, non-ARCHIVED task of this epic. Otherwise get_context isEpicFinal falls back to the highest order among the epic's non-ARCHIVED tasks, ties counting. It is optional, so epic files written before it load unchanged.
(b) The ProjectSettings qualityGateScope comment ('only on the epic's final task (highest order among siblings)') must name the designated final task, with that fallback.
(c) '## Validation Rules' > '### Epic' gets a finalTaskId bullet: optional, at most 200 chars, trimmed, '' clears; moe.update_epic refuses, before any write, an id that names no task, a task of another epic, or an ARCHIVED task.

docs/CONFIGURATION.md: in the qualityGateScope row (around line 183), replace '(highest `order` among siblings)'. The new text names the task get_context reports as isEpicFinal: the epic's finalTaskId (set with moe.update_epic), else the highest `order` among its non-ARCHIVED tasks.

Change nothing else in either file. Live tasks also declare them (SCHEMA.md: task-6b607b12 and task-fc9835fe; CONFIGURATION.md: task-bdf6db6f), so keep hunks small and leave every other line byte-identical. Use the CLI's own file-editing tool, not sed or shell writes: on a Claude seat, Edit/Write is the TOOL witness a contested path needs to land. Keep LF line endings. Docs tests read both files (executionContractDocs, daemonGitDocs, taskTimeBudgetDocs); remove no phrase they pin.

Adversarial self-review (load adversarial-self-review) of the six-file diff. Hunt for:
- any statement that contradicts isEpicFinalTask. The fallback is the highest order among NON-ARCHIVED tasks, ties counting. A designation is valid only while it names an existing, same-epic, non-ARCHIVED task. A task with no epic is final;
- any skill that still tells an agent to compare order via moe.list_tasks to learn its position;
- epic-breakdown missing either the immediate designation or the re-designation rule;
- skillFiles.ts changes outside the three entries;
- a qaCommitPolicy sentinel lost;
- unrelated hunks in the contested SCHEMA.md or CONFIGURATION.md;
- CRLF line endings;
- edits to .moe/skills, docs/MCP_SERVER.md or the moe-planning skill.
If any byte changes, re-run the step 4 gate fresh before complete_task. Report all six paths in complete_step.modifiedFiles, so the wrapper attributes them to this task.
